      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 64.44,
      "end": 67.06,
      "text": "Then the captain shook his head",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 69.04,
      "end": 75.06,
      "text": "Ellis got 9-11 with an empty case in by his bed",
      "uncertain": true
    },
    {
      "start": 77.32,
      "end": 81.0,
      "text": "Got not a ladder was the language",
      "uncertain": true
    },
    {
      "start": 82.22,
      "end": 86.1,
      "text": "Sharp and stupid, small and cold",
      "uncertain": true
    },
    {
      "start": 86.96,
      "end": 91.86,
      "text": "Something ugly kept us laughing when we couldn't stand at all",
      "uncertain": true
    },
    {
      "start": 91.86,
      "end": 96.84,
      "text": "Every joke became a bandage, every bandage soaked through air",
      "uncertain": true
    },
    {
      "start": 96.84,
      "end": 103.36,
      "text": "We kept saying got 9-11, so we didn't say our brothers did",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 107.2,
      "end": 112.62,
      "text": "Harlem worked the Kansas Station, hands still steady under fire",
      "uncertain": true
    },
    {
      "start": 112.62,
      "end": 116.38,
      "text": "The shell collapsed, the western ridge pole",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 116.38,
      "end": 119.02,
      "text": "Turned the white tent into a pyre",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 119.02,
      "end": 121.96,
      "text": "He had saved three men that evening",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 121.96,
      "end": 124.62,
      "text": "None could reach him where he bled",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
      "start": 125.58,
      "end": 127.54,
      "text": "Holland got 9-11",
      "uncertain": false
    },
    {
